jp2a
------------------------------------------
jp2a is a small utility that converts JPG images to ASCII. It's written in C
and released under the GPL.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libcurl4-8.22.0-1
  libexif12-0.6.26-1
  libjpeg8-3.2.0-1
  libncursesw10-6.5+20240427-1
  libpng16-1.6.59-1
  libwebp7-1.6.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libcurl-devel-8.22.0-1
  libexif-devel-0.6.26-1
  libjpeg-devel-3.2.0-1
  libncurses-devel-6.5+20240427-1
  libpng-devel-1.6.59-1
  libwebp-devel-1.6.0-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/Talinx/jp2a/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/Talinx/jp2a/archive/refs/tags/v1.3.3.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack jp2a-1.3.3-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./jp2a-1.3.3-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/jp2a-1.3.3-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/jp2a-1.3.3-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(jp2a)
  /etc/bash_completion.d/jp2a
  /usr/bin/jp2a.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/jp2a.README
